From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:46:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drv: report the package build identity as the module version

The MacBook9,1 package defines FTHD_SRCID as its version plus a hash of
the driver sources. Exposed through MODULE_VERSION it shows in modinfo
and in /sys/module/<name>/version, so a verifier can tell which source
the loaded module was built from. Builds without the define are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_drv.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fthd_drv.c b/fthd_drv.c
index b5431f3..e5cb70c 100644
--- a/fthd_drv.c
+++ b/fthd_drv.c
@@ -970,4 +970,12 @@ MODULE_FIRMWARE("facetimehd/9112_01XX.dat");
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(pci, fthd_pci_id_table);
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Patrik Jakobsson <patrik.r.jakobsson@gmail.com>");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("FacetimeHD camera driver");
+
+/*
+ * A package build passes its version and a hash of these sources, so that
+ * the loaded module (/sys/module/<name>/version) can be traced to its source.
+ */
+#ifdef FTHD_SRCID
+MODULE_VERSION(FTHD_SRCID);
+#endif
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
-- 
